From tru64-unix-managers  Wed Dec 27 19:56:24 2000
From: Andrew Shinn <Andrew.Shinn () Wiznet ! com>
Date: Wed, 27 Dec 2000 19:56:24 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: SUMMARY:  Strange Tru64 Networking Issue
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=97794707009621

It ended up being a DUPLEX PROBLEM after all.. It would appear the ifconfig
speed commands (IE: ifconfig ee0 up speed 200) don't work so hot.

So on the suggestion of Larry Clegg and Sean O'Connell I added the following
line to /etc/inet.local : 

/usr/sbin/lan_config -i ee0 -a 0 -s 100 -x 1
                       ^      ^       ^\    ^\
                     iface medium(utp) speed  duplex(on/full)

rebooted the host and voila.. here are the speeds I now get to the NT/Linux
hosts :

ncftp / > put vmunix
vmunix:                                                 14.89 MB    10.71
MB/s


Thanks everyone and have a Happy New Year.

-Andrew Shinn
andrew.shinn@wiznet.com

