We found the answer.   The SCSI target id we were trying to assign for the 2
devices were 5 and 6.

6 was in use on SystemA as the SCSI id of the card.   I imagine that in  a
cluster the SCSI id of the cards needs to be different.

We changed the target id of the device configured to use 6.0 to use 5.1
instead, leaving the SCSI card ids at 7 and 6.

Many thanks for the software engineer ( Abbot / Cork, Ireland) from EMC for
helping me find/fix the problem.

