Subject: FW: SUMMARY: Firmaware for 5.1 on a 20E
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=97747175625881

NO NO NO, Ultra3 is backward compatible with Ultra2 and Ultra.  It is
designed that way.

I would have stayed with Ultra3 {160 Mbit/s}. Your problem was, SCSI
controller, Cables, Terminators, Firmware, Differential SCSI, etc.  Why
replace drives when you could have replaced the card.

Ultra2 is only 80 Mbit/s. You just lost about half burst trough put.

Anyway, AFAIK Ultra2 drives are not manufactured any more {Well I cant get
any stock, all are Ultra3}.  So you just got new hardware {Old stock} that
can only be replaced by Ultra3.  

All our drives are Ultra3 on HSG80/Drive Cage that is Ultra2 only and no
problems. In future I just upgrade the drive cage.

Hope it helps.



-----Original Message-----
From: BrianH@dice.com [mailto:BrianH@dice.com]
Sent: Friday, 22 December, 2000 1:49 AM
To: BrianH@dice.com; tru64-unix-managers@ornl.gov
Subject: SUMMARY: Firmaware for 5.1 on a 20E


Well it turns out the whole problem resulted from our reseller putting the
wrong scsi card in our server.  The drives were Ultra3, but the card was
Ultra2.  I replaced the drives with Ultra2 ones, and everything installs
fine now.

--Brian

