From tru64-unix-managers  Thu Dec 14 22:48:16 2000
From: BrianH () dice ! com
Date: Thu, 14 Dec 2000 22:48:16 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: SUMMARY: Installing 5.1 on a Third Party Alpha
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=97683417006183

Thanks to:
John J. Francini [francini@zk3.dec.com]

After a little discovery, it turns out that Linux was on the drive before
Tru64.  Linux writes is master boot record to block 0 of the drive.  Tru64
needs to write dsk0a to that block so they were conflicting.  I reformatted
the drive under DOS and did and fdisk /mbr and now am installing 5.1 just
fine.

Thanks
--Brian

