Thanks to all who responded 

How do I enforce a password lifetime of (n days) for all
current users and subsequent users ?

This response from Larye D.Parkins did it for me..

/etc/auth/system/default:
 :d_pw_expire_warning#xxxxx:\
where xxxxx is the warning time before expiration

existing accounts:  use usermod to add -x u_exp=#xxxxx
where xxxxx is the password lifetime following a change.  Or, use u_life to
set
the absolute password lifetime.

new accounts:  add the u_exp line to the default database so they will be
created with an expiration time

(you must be running with Enhanced Security to use the password aging). 



