From tru64-unix-managers  Wed Dec 13 22:02:05 2000
From: Ken Kleiner <ken () cs ! uml ! edu>
Date: Wed, 13 Dec 2000 22:02:05 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: SUMMARY : Networker / index problem...
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=97674571918329

Hello...

 I solved my previous problem that I posted about.  I thought I had 
networker index corruption (I sort of did) that was stopping nsrd from
running, giving errors from nsrmmdbd.  The problem was that my media
index directory was hosed up by fsck (we had a system crash due to
power failure).  What I did was look at another networker server's 
/var/nsr/mm directory and noticed that my server's directory had 
a file or 2 missing/corrupted.  I created them (they were 0 length)
and then nsrd started up for me.

  After this, I had to do a mmrecov to get the latest media index back
off of tape.

  Things are up now!

