Yes, easy.

Edit /etc/profile and add at end of file:  
LOGCNT=`w | grep $LOGNAME | wc -l`
if [ "$LOGCNT" -gt "1" ] ; then
    clear
    echo "\n The user - $LOGNAME - has already logged on ..."
    exit
fi


