Hi

DO NOT ISSUE THE CONSVAR -G EWA0_MODE COMMAND.

Our setup includes two dec alpha DS20E (System A and System B) 
that are in a clustered environment (V1.6)

We found the consvar command and read the man pages and 
did a consvar -l and sure enough the ewa0_mode variable was not there.  

But we new it existed. We tried consvar -l ewa0_mode and the 
variable and its setting are listed.  So if we can see it, we should be able
to set it.

consvar -g ewa_mode <value>. return 

This is a really really bad thing to do, we not only crashed the system we
issued our command
on, but the other member crashed due to a scsi bus timeout.

It turns out if the variable does not show up in the "consvar -l" command do
not try to
set it.

We have since found out from compaq that is a undocumented feature, and they
are going
to update the man page appropriately

Darren


